{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-124180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-1$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $x,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(-1)-4 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "27bb0909fa0edafeae2316c4e0da58338f27fc125d56995182b9d8586cc03ef6"} {"question" "q-124180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["text" "Impossible to determine"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=9$ and ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-3,$ calculate ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ -{\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-3-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ -9 & =-3-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\ -6 & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "27bb0909fa0edafeae2316c4e0da58338f27fc125d56995182b9d8586cc03ef6"} {"question" "q-124185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124185" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/assets/9c42d875a65a6b54ad7769180f5ec2e831772ad44a89ec913951da40c6d90514.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y,$ where $C$ is the path along the line segment between the points $(-3,0)$ to the point $(0,2),$ as shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The line integral of unity with respect to $y$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $y$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{2}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${y}_{1}$ is the $y$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{2}=2$ and ${y}_{1}=0.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}y={y}_{2}-{y}_{1}=2-0=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f04b2c158f0c267181644cb1bc09b4ef1424259c659775965c4bccdd038bdc9"} {"question" "q-124334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079767/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "27bb0909fa0edafeae2316c4e0da58338f27fc125d56995182b9d8586cc03ef6"} {"question" "q-124334" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" 